			"widgets_values":[
				"integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action, cinematic, a wide tracking shot follows a male skier carving down a steep, sunlit alpine powder slope, with jagged snow-capped peaks and a pale blue winter sky filling the background. He wears a fitted red-and-black ski jacket, black insulated pants, a black helmet, and red-tinted goggles; a light layer of powder sprays off his skis as he pumps through a series of aggressive carved turns, gaining speed toward a natural snow ramp at the bottom of the pitch. The camera trucks right with small amplitude at medium speed, keeping his crouched, athletic silhouette framed against the bright snowfield. [Shot 2] At 00:02.000, the shot cuts to a low-angle wide shot at the lip of the snow ramp. The skier hits the takeoff at full speed, launches off the edge, and snaps into a backward rotation; his knees tuck to his chest, his arms fold in tight, and his skis stay parallel as his body rotates a full backflip in the air. The camera holds a static shot as he passes the apex of the rotation, snow crystals from the takeoff glittering in the sunlight around his silhouette, the mountain range wheeling behind him through the upside-down arc. [Shot 3] At 00:04.500, the shot cuts to a high-angle side shot of the landing zone. He completes the final quarter of the rotation, extends his body, and lands in a smooth forward stance on the packed snow below; his skis carve a clean arc as he absorbs the impact with bent knees, throwing up a wide fan of powder to either side. He glides out of the landing, straightens upright, and skis away across the open slope, leaving a single clean track trailing behind him in the untouched powder. The camera pans left with small amplitude at slow speed, tracking him until he shrinks into the distance of the white valley.\n\noverall_soundscape: Cold wind rushes past the skis with a rising whistle during the descent, while the edges of the skis hiss and scrape against the packed snow with each carved turn. The takeoff produces a sharp scuff and a brief silence at the apex of the flip, followed by a crisp, damp thud on landing and the soft rustle of sprayed powder settling back onto the snowfield.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A driving electronic beat at a fast tempo with a pulsing synth-bass line builds through the descent, cuts to a thin, suspended synth pad during the airborne backflip, then resolves into a heavy drop with layered percussion and a rising chord as he lands and skis away.\n",
				1344,
				768,
				124
